pi.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":20891,"digest":"sha256:16b624f0af8a6af80cf4e6f20dc8ee70b02929634bd0a5c5fd46a264ebe2a82b","download_count":1445,"created_at":"2026-10-23T10:51:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T10:51:07Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/releases/download/v1.27.0/packslip.sigstore.json"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/releases/assets/668828023","id":668828023,"node_id":"RA_kwDOT-nLJc4n3YF3","name":"SHA256SUMS","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":705,"digest":"sha256:2c6255c3620454bc6a7c98ab615e5dad909a0003b132fb824f59a4a86bbf9fe1","download_count":34,"created_at":"2026-10-23T10:50:40Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T10:50:40Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/releases/download/v1.27.0/SHA256SUMS"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/tarball/v1.27.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/zipball/v1.27.0","body":"Garbage collection can now remove cold incremental sessions from checkouts that are in use. Incremental seeding no longer changes the donor checkout's files, which fixes optimized builds that failed to link. This release also stops object files piling up in target directories on macOS and fixes cache problems across worktrees and on Windows. The first build after upgrading discards older learned incremental state once and reruns each build script once; see **Upgrade notes**.\n\n## Added\n\n- **gc trims learned incremental state in checkouts that are in use** ([#776](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/776), @ViRb3). Before, a worktree built all day never had its incremental state collected, so it could grow well past `gc.incremental_max_size`. Now gc deletes that checkout's finished rustc sessions, oldest first, until the budget is met. It takes rustc's own session lock before deleting a session and never removes unit directories or sessions in progress. A compile that starts just as its newest session is deleted builds that unit from scratch once.\n  - Cache hits now count as use, so a unit restored from the cache on every build no longer looks cold. Seeding copies from the checkout that used a unit most recently.\n  - When gc is over budget, it keeps units used in the last hour. It still removes them if they have expired, take up more than half the budget, or the disk is below `gc.min_free_size`.\n  - Files hard-linked between sessions are counted once, and only when their last link is removed.\n  - `mbx gc` reports `removed N sessions from M learned incremental units in live checkouts` and `kept K learned incremental units used in the last hour`. `mbx gc --json` adds `removed_sessions`, `session_units` and `kept_hot_units` under `incremental`. No settings were added or changed.\n\n## Fixed\n\n- **Incremental seeding no longer breaks the donor checkout's next link** ([#789](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/789), @jbellis). With seeding on (the default since 1.26.0 with rustc 1.98+), an optimized build could fail in the checkout that donated state with `rust-lld: error: undefined hidden symbol`, and only `mbx clean` fixed it. Seeding hard-linked the donor's session files, and rustc rewrites some of them in place, such as ThinLTO bitcode. Now each seeded file gets its own copy: a reflink on Linux (Btrfs, XFS, ZFS with block cloning), `clonefile` on macOS, or a plain copy where the filesystem can't clone. Seeding is a bit slower and plain copies use extra disk, and gc now counts each seeded copy on its own.\n- **Target directories no longer fill with old object files on macOS** ([#791](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/791), @ViRb3). With `split-debuginfo = \"unpacked\"`, which Cargo uses on macOS for the default `dev` and `test` profiles, every compile left a full new set of `*.rcgu.o` files in `deps/`, and nothing deleted them. In mbx's own repository they took 8.7 GiB of a 9.5 GiB target. After a successful compile through mbx, the unit's object files from earlier compiles are now deleted, so each unit keeps at most its last few compiles' objects. Files that the debug info still points to are kept. Nothing is deleted after a failed compile or under `-C save-temps`. Linux and Windows are unchanged, because rustc already deletes these files there.\n- **Cached build-script output no longer points into another worktree's target** ([#790](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/790), @jbellis). If a build script canonicalized `OUT_DIR` and printed the result, for example in `cargo:rustc-env=...`, the cached output kept the first worktree's resolved managed-target path. A second worktree that restored it read the first worktree's files, or failed once they were gone. mbx now also normalizes resolved paths, so restored output names the receiving checkout's own `target/...`.\n- **`mbx cache import` keeps existing results when a bundle conflicts** ([#781](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/781), @jbellis). Importing into a store that wasn't empty could fail with `local action key already has a different result`. When that happened with a directory bundle, the bundle couldn't be imported again. Now import keeps intact existing results, the same way publishing does, and imports the rest of the bundle. An existing result with missing or truncated outputs is still replaced. Imports into an empty store, such as on fresh CI runners, behave as before.\n- **Cargo wrapper loops now stop with an error** ([#788](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/788), @jdx). If mbx's Cargo shim picked a Cargo that runs mbx again, it used to start new processes forever. One example is a mise `[wrappers.cargo]` entry combined with a custom `cargo` script that runs mbx. The shim now stops after 12 nested entries. The error names the selected Cargo, says whether it came from `CARGO` or `PATH`, and suggests pointing the outer wrapper at the real Cargo.\n- **Build-script caching works on native Windows** ([#787](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/787), @jdx). Cargo starts build scripts without the `.exe` extension, so mbx couldn't find the preserved original. It printed its own help and exited with code 2, which failed the build at the first crate with a build script, such as proc-macro2 or quote.\n- **`mbx rustc --print` works** ([#780](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/780), @jbellis). Nightly commands such as `mbx rustc --print=cfg -Z unstable-options --lib` were wrongly rejected with an error saying mbx was set as Cargo's rustc wrapper. Setting `RUSTC_WRAPPER=mbx` still gives that error.\n\n## Upgrade notes\n\n- **Older learned incremental state is discarded once** ([#789](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/789)). Hard links made by older versions stay after the upgrade, and there's no way to tell which state was already overwritten. So the first build on 1.27.0 discards all learned incremental state from older versions, and the next collection deletes it. If another build is using a checkout at that moment, mbx discards its state at a later build once the checkout is idle. Seeding stays off until all of that state is gone. Expect one cold incremental compile per checkout. **Stop builds running older mbx versions before you upgrade**, because they can still create shared files.\n- **Build scripts run once more** ([#790](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/790)). The build-script execution cache version went from 4 to 5, so results cached by earlier versions aren't reused.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/compare/v1.26.0...v1.27.0","mentions_count":3}